[{:db/id "q-317527/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "ed5e8751-13e3-58d5-abe6-987115bcbc57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317527/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d30facd2-44cc-58de-8518-e9b64a44e5de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317527/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-317527/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317527/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "32524c49-9cdf-558b-a997-d86741880778" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317527/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b50fced-d890-525d-ac5f-a89dd2091246" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317527/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-317527/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317527" :question/id #uuid "3a8832a3-1f6e-5ad2-9d95-30c944ab7d15" :question/math-academy-id "q-317527" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(2)(1)-(1)(-2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317527/field-1" "q-317527/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317509/field-1/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "d824e97e-c767-5491-9b27-57197b58eefb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317509/field-1/8ca4b7a1e89c730869f48c3a3ace0473b36e7c19c70ef8efef65592fedc719dd" :answer/id #uuid "a021e344-a3d3-5d81-8d0d-71a821517f14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317509/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "46cc790d-e372-586c-9565-30757ab035be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317509/field-1/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer-field/choices ["q-317509/field-1/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" "q-317509/field-1/8ca4b7a1e89c730869f48c3a3ace0473b36e7c19c70ef8efef65592fedc719dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317509/field-2/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "f2bd5967-0a06-5e5f-90ed-f30f5110edfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317509/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "42cc3774-b7a2-5d8e-ab2e-f8af50711a34" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317509/field-2/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer-field/choices ["q-317509/field-2/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317509" :question/id #uuid "4055556b-4590-59c0-ae15-eb16a5349d24" :question/math-academy-id "q-317509" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(2)(3)-(5)(1)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}45 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317509/field-1" "q-317509/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317509"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317436/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "be4844fc-62f3-5141-b816-71872e8421ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317436/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "87a3bcfe-7825-5a70-9588-8df57bd4628c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317436/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-317436/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317436/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "0674fdce-1eea-5b24-8118-caf0022c70b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317436/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f82772f8-6514-5852-b19f-dd8ff12e84c9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317436/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-317436/field-2/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317436" :question/id #uuid "daabe69c-e766-509d-b9e2-4798548ebdd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-317436" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(2)(7)-(3)(5)}[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317436/field-1" "q-317436/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317436"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-159976/selection/c87615c8ca70fd83c2dbb380cf667fd8a0c153d05689ea5ad0b2b4d3b0ad2a84" :answer/id #uuid "c1623742-720f-5587-8a47-bb862da3c90b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159976/selection/b850599e940b61fffd431fafe2dbd1ce8f434da6657e815842d66375d23a0c0d" :answer/id #uuid "ab033076-8953-5871-8f32-7ff067cc6efb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159976/selection/56ee719339db84264fd149d3d5b853351fe7cf4db467fe51505b180a7988a149" :answer/id #uuid "ea134e61-c8d9-53cb-a23a-5bc511acea18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159976/selection/bb16bc6ce7c2149a97b873bda7b1a09bc9b46df8f0f42f7383b17635a51e017e" :answer/id #uuid "5b133e34-4c9f-5ad6-a358-860b7fea8775" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159976/selection/913866f386fea281b2465403bf3fd1a386017c8fb1fd5c4a0f9065a84a89976c" :answer/id #uuid "c9191c81-8d89-5a0a-aa75-d912b0acb792" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-159976/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b72f55c3-a9f5-53af-8ae7-73804f476f68" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-159976/selection/c87615c8ca70fd83c2dbb380cf667fd8a0c153d05689ea5ad0b2b4d3b0ad2a84" :answer-field/choices ["q-159976/selection/c87615c8ca70fd83c2dbb380cf667fd8a0c153d05689ea5ad0b2b4d3b0ad2a84" "q-159976/selection/b850599e940b61fffd431fafe2dbd1ce8f434da6657e815842d66375d23a0c0d" "q-159976/selection/56ee719339db84264fd149d3d5b853351fe7cf4db467fe51505b180a7988a149" "q-159976/selection/bb16bc6ce7c2149a97b873bda7b1a09bc9b46df8f0f42f7383b17635a51e017e" "q-159976/selection/913866f386fea281b2465403bf3fd1a386017c8fb1fd5c4a0f9065a84a89976c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-159976" :question/id #uuid "ede69c8f-2758-5c85-a62b-6b678eca588f" :question/math-academy-id "q-159976" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-6-(-4)}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-159976/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-159976"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-317438/field-1/32b041f2c12a070b2fda6a5b955b34d8f4482fc8b309a639df4220ce65c6f6b9" :answer/id #uuid "8089a1d0-6679-50aa-bd62-eb14a62b9918" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{19}{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317438/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f4011f-2573-5a29-9e26-2cc40329b2f3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317438/field-1/32b041f2c12a070b2fda6a5b955b34d8f4482fc8b309a639df4220ce65c6f6b9" :answer-field/choices ["q-317438/field-1/32b041f2c12a070b2fda6a5b955b34d8f4482fc8b309a639df4220ce65c6f6b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317438/field-2/fba3f071a3bf374a14af37c3a2bf03fdd1045070379d4ec39535030fd010d58a" :answer/id #uuid "c4a4f791-56a7-50ec-a84c-80bf0e0892d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317438/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed0e9aa5-4f2e-5458-8c6a-d30d263064a6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317438/field-2/fba3f071a3bf374a14af37c3a2bf03fdd1045070379d4ec39535030fd010d58a" :answer-field/choices ["q-317438/field-2/fba3f071a3bf374a14af37c3a2bf03fdd1045070379d4ec39535030fd010d58a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317438" :question/id #uuid "2a5b1916-5c8e-5d27-97ff-8d340265e87c" :question/math-academy-id "q-317438" :question/problem "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\nv={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{12+2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{14}[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{19}{14} \\\\ \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317438/field-1" "q-317438/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4daa6bc-1c9a-5c23-8032-4d70435d9388"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-9265"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(0,2),(-3,3),(12,4),$ and $(7,3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n\n- $(-2,2)$\n- $(1,-1)$\n- $(4,4)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 12 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -6 & 8 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 8 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(-1,2),(-3,3),(4,4),(2,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-9261/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "f5946870-2d6f-5935-b5a7-c3a8b5858647" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9261/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "2babb4b4-8f0d-57c3-8297-895b786e58bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9261/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "f5e5a627-06d5-5003-b4a6-04bb238b5139" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9261/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "12d84ba8-cebd-5af1-b1f9-765411778e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9261/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "046c48f1-f1e3-54af-804d-9857c6468857" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9261/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab418508-d416-56ee-a77b-2aedc68c706a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9261/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-9261/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-9261/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-9261/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-9261/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-9261/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9261" :question/id #uuid "bf6e11d8-5ea3-59be-827c-ae219c307f71" :question/math-academy-id "q-9261" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe parallelogram $P$ is mapped to the parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The parallelogram ${P}^{′}$ has vertices $(-2,2),(-5,4),(-3,2),$ and $(0,0).$ Which of the following are vertices of $P?$\n\n- $(-2,1)$\n- $(0,0)$\n- $(2,0)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${P}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $P$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3-2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of $P$ are $(0,2),(-1,2),(-1,0),(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-9261/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9261"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85172/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "98744a46-1ddc-5d16-939d-fc52da67c11f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85172/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f3e6c023-fced-5e51-9290-8d99c38b7209" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85172/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "0f0cf815-df8d-5406-801e-49e27bdf5726" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85172/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a816077d-0b79-5326-b761-d4032a5bdc86" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85172/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "27b17022-e430-5321-a4f4-dcc39497578a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85172/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "da278268-0953-57c8-8371-23abd5230202" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85172/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-85172/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-85172/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-85172/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-85172/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-85172/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85172" :question/id #uuid "cf0d1bd1-6767-5355-bf10-b6a1baf057d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-85172" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(10,5),(0,-5),$ and $(15,20).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(9,5)$\n- $(0,1)$\n- $(10,-7)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{35-30}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -10 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 & 15 \\\\ 5 & -5 & 20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 50 & -125 \\\\ 5 & -35 & 95\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 10 & -25 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 19\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(0,1),(10,-7),(-25,19).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-85172/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85172"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9260/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "0fffd738-4cc0-5bf4-9acf-ffc1c3a5cbc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9260/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "c2f7e9b7-308f-5313-b11f-5a207e849432" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9260/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "97cfc117-8119-5358-b40e-1969d823667b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9260/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "d82cd06c-e45b-58bd-aa6e-dbe87a7fe4ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9260/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "7bb88d0a-ce48-5029-91dc-f4ad6cae1502" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9260/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a114fd5-7e4d-5459-9cdc-28ea458efd72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9260/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-9260/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-9260/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-9260/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-9260/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-9260/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9260" :question/id #uuid "d16ef5a3-3a6f-5da6-b7af-bd2013438501" :question/math-academy-id "q-9260" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(-21,0),(21,0),$ and $(0,3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(0,-3)$\n- $(3,1)$\n- $(-3,3)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-7-0}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}-21 & 21 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -21\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-3,0),(3,0),(0,-3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9260/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9260"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-9255/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d909f321-0332-526d-b496-6ace0c6f7579" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9255/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "e46f312a-9b66-5ace-a5f8-651db7728461" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9255/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "91f5c48f-d05f-5cff-90ae-d12bfc8eb888" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9255/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "28e3ef56-12f4-504b-801b-f27f1626be7b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9255/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "54c30f94-9552-5c2a-80c6-1245bbc63410" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9255/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "765daac3-6ce4-521c-ba95-5db5eea21b30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-9255/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-9255/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-9255/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-9255/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-9255/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-9255/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-9255" :question/id #uuid "187a3494-862e-562d-b358-18813743f678" :question/math-academy-id "q-9255" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle ${S}^{′}$ under the action of $T.$ The triangle ${S}^{′}$ has vertices $(3,2),(14,6),$ and $(9,2).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(3,2)$\n- $(1,1)$\n- $(5,1)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of ${S}^{′}:$ \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 14 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(-1,1),(2,3),(5,1).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9255/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9255"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5466"] :question/problem "The vector $\\mathbf{v}$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 10 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $\\mathbf{v}?$" :question/worked-solution "From the given information, we have\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by $T^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-15-(-20)}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -10 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -10 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5467"] :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe triangle $S$ is mapped to the triangle $S'$ under the action of $\\mathbf T.$ The triangle $S'$ has vertices $(4,3),(4,10),$ and $(-4,-3).$ Which of the following are vertices of $S?$\n\n- $(1,0)$\n\n- $(4,-3)$\n\n- $(-1,0)$" :question/worked-solution "First, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of $S'\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of $S$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by $T^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4-(-3)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 10 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}7 & 14 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 28 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, the coordinates of the vertices of the original triangle are $(1,0),(2,4),(-1,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
